Subject: [PATCH] Recheck actual Camera processor release after a timed wait

A timed condition wait may return false after the processor has actually
been released while the waiter reacquires the lock. Recheck the predicate,
not just the timer result. Notify every waiter; each still checks the same
locked predicate. Keep the seven-second failure for a genuinely busy
processor, retain releaseNodeChain, and do not force-free native buffers.
This addresses the Java wait race, not a lost native release callback.

--- a/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/camera/core2/processor/PictureProcessorManager.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/samsung/android/camera/core2/processor/PictureProcessorManager.smali
@@ -1248,7 +1248,7 @@
     :goto_0
     iget-object v1, p0, Lcom/samsung/android/camera/core2/processor/PictureProcessorManager;->mImmediateProcessorReleaseCond:Ljava/util/concurrent/locks/Condition;
 
-    invoke-interface {v1}, Ljava/util/concurrent/locks/Condition;->signal()V
+    invoke-interface {v1}, Ljava/util/concurrent/locks/Condition;->signalAll()V
 
     const-string v1, "deinitialize X"
 
@@ -1453,8 +1453,12 @@
 
     goto :goto_0
 
-    :cond_0
-    new-instance p1, Lcom/samsung/android/camera/core2/exception/InvalidOperationException;
+    :cond_0
+    iget-object v0, p0, Lcom/samsung/android/camera/core2/processor/PictureProcessorManager;->mImmediateProcessor:Lcom/samsung/android/camera/core2/processor/ImmediateProcessor;
+
+    if-eqz v0, :cond_1
+
+    new-instance p1, Lcom/samsung/android/camera/core2/exception/InvalidOperationException;
 
     sget-object p2, Ljava/util/Locale;->UK:Ljava/util/Locale;
 
